  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThere's a [list of DTDs](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#parsing-xhtml-documents%3Anamed-character-references) in the HTML standard that is used for which DTDs get certain entities supported (I think).\n\nThe [relevant Firefox code](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/d87eb30d610a3032111f9ee47441b53927de63d3/parser/htmlparser/nsExpatDriver.cpp#291) matches this list, whereas the [relevant WebKit code](https://searchfox.org/wubkat/rev/919691a4ebb09a93c2dc093686cdc284e35ff623/Source/WebCore/xml/parser/XMLDocumentParserLibxml2.cpp#1293) and [relevant Chromium code](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/xml/parser/xml_document_parser.cc;l=1581;drc=0e0e8cb1abd6e24fb231327f73031820cad67f2b) have two additional public IDs that were added in [this change in 2013](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/a731872538f382141594b14c324a134503481dd8%5E%21):\n* `\"-//WAPFORUM//DTD XHTML Mobile 1.1//EN\"`\n* `\"-//WAPFORUM//DTD XHTML Mobile 1.2//EN\"`\n\nI suspect at this point the path of least resistance may be to make a change to the spec corresponding to the 2013 change.  cc: @smaug---- @hsivonen \n",
